{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.1", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.1"}, "paraphrase": "All beings have buddha-nature, because the dharmakāya of the buddhas pervades them, because suchness is undifferentiated, and because the potential (gotra) is present (following the Ratnagotravibhāga). The potential is presented in five kinds — cut off, uncertain, śrāvaka, pratyekabuddha and Mahāyāna — and even the 'cut off' are not cut off forever.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:tathagatagarbha", "trm:gotra"], "concepts": ["cpt:buddha-nature"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally. Chapter number per the usual 21-chapter division.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.12", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.12"}, "paraphrase": "The perfection of generosity is threefold: giving material things, giving Dharma, and giving protection from fear; it is perfected by being joined with wisdom.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ethics"], "terms": ["trm:paramita", "trm:dana"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-paramitas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.15", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.15"}, "paraphrase": "The perfection of diligence overcomes three kinds of laziness: the laziness of idleness, of discouragement (thinking oneself incapable), and of attachment to unworthy activities.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:virya"], "concepts": ["cpt:six-paramitas"], "obstacles": ["obs:three-kinds-of-laziness"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.17", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.17"}, "paraphrase": "The perfection of wisdom realizes the selflessness of persons and of phenomena; phenomena are neither existent nor non-existent; what is realized is free of the extremes, and meditation is resting without grasping in that.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:prajna", "trm:sunyata"], "concepts": ["cpt:two-selflessnesses", "cpt:six-paramitas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.18", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.18"}, "paraphrase": "The five paths — accumulation, joining, seeing, meditation, and no-more-learning — describe the progress from the first generation of bodhicitta to buddhahood.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "paths": ["pth:five-paths"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.19", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.19"}, "paraphrase": "The ten grounds of the bodhisattva, from the Very Joyful to the Cloud of Dharma, followed by the ground of buddhahood.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:bhumi"], "paths": ["pth:ten-bhumis"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.2", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.2"}, "paraphrase": "The precious human life is the working basis: it has the eight freedoms and ten endowments, is hard to obtain and easily lost; it must be joined with three kinds of faith (clear, longing, confident).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "terms": ["trm:ksanasampad", "trm:sraddha"], "concepts": ["cpt:eight-freedoms-and-ten-endowments", "cpt:four-thoughts-that-turn-the-mind"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.20", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.20"}, "paraphrase": "Perfect buddhahood is the three kāyas: the dharmakāya for one's own benefit, the saṃbhogakāya and nirmāṇakāya for others' benefit.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:dharmakaya", "trm:sambhogakaya", "trm:nirmanakaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-kayas"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.21", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.21"}, "paraphrase": "The activity of the buddhas benefits beings spontaneously and without conceptual thought, like the sun shining or a wish-fulfilling jewel.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.3", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.3"}, "paraphrase": "Without a spiritual friend one cannot reach buddhahood, as a traveller needs a guide, an escort and a ferryman. The kind of spiritual friend matches the disciple's level: for a beginner, an ordinary person as spiritual friend; for one whose karmic obscurations are largely purified, a bodhisattva on the grounds; on the great path of accumulation, a nirmāṇakāya buddha; on the grounds, a saṃbhogakāya buddha.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "terms": ["trm:kalyanamitra"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-kinds-of-spiritual-friend", "cpt:guru"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally. The correlation of friend-types with stages is recalled in substance; check the exact stage names.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.4", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.4"}, "paraphrase": "Impermanence: the outer world and the beings in it are impermanent; death is certain and its time uncertain; contemplating this turns the mind from the concerns of this life.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["death-dying", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-thoughts-that-turn-the-mind"], "practices": ["prc:four-thoughts-that-turn-the-mind"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.5", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.5"}, "paraphrase": "The suffering of saṃsāra: the suffering of suffering, the suffering of change, and the all-pervading suffering of conditioned existence, described for each of the six realms.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["world-fate", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-kinds-of-suffering", "cpt:rebirth-realms"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.6", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.6"}, "paraphrase": "Karma and its result: non-virtuous, virtuous and unmoving actions; the ten non-virtues and their fully ripened results, results similar to the cause and environmental results; actions are certain to ripen on their doer.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["action"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ethics"], "terms": ["trm:karma"], "concepts": ["cpt:karma"], "obstacles": ["obs:ten-akusala-kammapatha"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.7", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.7"}, "paraphrase": "Love and compassion are each of three kinds: with beings as object, with phenomena as object, and without object.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ethics"], "terms": ["trm:karuna", "trm:maitri"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-immeasurables-mahayana"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.8", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.8"}, "paraphrase": "Refuge in the Buddha, Dharma and Saṅgha is the foundation of all vows; its causes are fear and faith (for the Mahāyāna, compassion); its trainings are described.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "terms": ["trm:saranagamana"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-refuges"], "practices": ["prc:refuge-prostrations"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:ch.9", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "ch.9"}, "paraphrase": "Bodhicitta — the wish for perfect awakening for the sake of others — is of two kinds, aspiring and engaging, and relative and ultimate; it is taken as a vow in a ritual.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ethics", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:bodhicitta"], "practices": ["prc:bodhicittotpada", "prc:bodhisattva-vow"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jewel-ornament-of-liberation:intro", "source": "src:jewel-ornament-of-liberation", "location": {"ref": "intro"}, "paraphrase": "The whole path is summarized under six headings: the cause is buddha-nature; the basis is the precious human life; the condition is the spiritual friend; the method is the spiritual friend's instructions; the result is the kāyas of perfect buddhahood; the activity is benefiting beings without conceptual thought.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:jewel-ornament-six-topics"], "paths": ["pth:jewel-ornament-sequence"], "teachers": ["tch:gampopa"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U46-kagyu"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Reference from memory; the text is not available locally. The summary verse at the opening of the text; exact wording not reproduced.", "coverage": ["B6"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U46-kagyu"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
